  "answer_text": "It looks like there are several pools named \"Glenwood Pool\" in different locations! Here's a summary of the most notable ones:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfca 1. Glenwood Pool \u2013 Forest Glen, Maryland\nGlenwood Pool is a swim club set back among the trees and along a creek in historic Forest Glen, Maryland. You can contact them at board@glenwoodpool.org for more information.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf21\ufe0f 2. Glenwood Hot Springs Resort \u2013 Glenwood Springs, Colorado\nGlenwood Hot Springs Resort has more than 7 expansive pools on the property, including the original historic pool which is the \"world's largest hot springs pool.\" The historic thermal spring water has been drawing visitors from all over the world since 1888.\n\n- The source of the mineral water is the Yampah Spring, which produces over 3.5 million gallons of water per day at a temperature of 122\u00b0F.\n- The Grand Pool contains over 1 million gallons of water and is an aquatic playing field for kids of all ages.\n- Pass options include full access to all pools, including the Grand Pool, the Hot Therapy Pool, Sopris Splash Zone, and Hanging Lake Falls Pool.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfca 3. Glenwood Aquatic Center \u2013 Glenwood Springs, CO (Parks & Recreation)\nThis 277,000-gallon pool boasts 8 lap lanes and a one-meter diving board, ranging from 4 feet to 12 feet deep, with a temperature kept between 82\u201384 degrees. It is located at 100 Wulfsohn Road, Glenwood Springs, CO 81601.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfca 4. Glenwood Pool \u2013 Columbus, Ohio\nGlenwood Pool in Columbus opens for the season May 23. Admission is $3 and a leisure card is required for entry.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfca 5. Glennwood Pool \u2013 Evans, Georgia\nGlennwood Pool is a non-profit, volunteer-run neighborhood pool in Evans, Georgia, offering memberships for residents and non-residents, seasonal events like dive-in movie nights, military & senior discounts, and a welcoming space for families.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfca 6. Glenwood Houses Pool \u2013 Brooklyn, New York\nLocated in the Glenwood Houses neighborhood of Brooklyn, New York, the Glenwood Houses Pool offers a place to cool off and enjoy the water during the hot New York summers. Managed by NYC Parks, it is a well-maintained facility that caters to the community's aquatic needs.\n\n---\n\nCould you clarify which **Glenwood Pool** you're looking for? I'd be happy to provide more specific details! \ud83d\ude0a",
